  "details": "https://creators.vrchat.com/avatars/shader-fallback-system/\n\n\"DoubleSided\n\nHidden //(this will hide the mesh from view if the shader is blocked, useful for things like raymarching effects.\"\n\n1. Change VRCFallback  tag value to \"Hidden\". \n\n2. Expected behaviour: when shaders is blocked, a mesh with this shader should not be visible.\n\n3. Invite a friend and ask them to block your shaders in safety.\n\n4. Mesh is still visible after blocking. \n\nI am not sure yet if this impacts all shaders, but observed it with poiyomi.\n\nVRCFallback behaviour should be independent from shader so i expect this spreads to all shaders.\n\nUnless I did something wrong, but then the doc seems to be incomplete.\n\nOr perhaps this is not available on currently allowed old unity\n\n2019.4.31f1 but will work with new Unity version? This is just a guess and apply only to SDK, as game already migrated...",
